    {
      "name": "Debugging & Monitoring",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "View Kafka Topics (Linux/Mac)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://example.com",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": ["example", "com"]
            },
            "description": "To view Kafka topics and messages, run these commands in your terminal:\n\n```bash\n# List all topics\nkafka-topics --list --bootstrap-server localhost:9092\n\n# Describe the booking-updates topic\nkafka-topics --describe --topic booking-updates --bootstrap-server localhost:9092\n\n# Monitor messages in real-time\nkafka-console-consumer --topic booking-updates --from-beginning --bootstrap-server localhost:9092\n```\n\nYou should see BookingEvent messages with flightId, passengerCount, and isBusinessClass."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Booking Service Logs Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://example.com",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": ["example", "com"]
            },
            "description": "Check booking service logs for:\n\n1. **Kafka Connection**: Look for messages like \"Kafka producer configured\" or connection errors\n2. **Event Publishing**: Look for \"Booking event sent to Kafka\"\n3. **Errors**: Any socket or serialization errors\n\nCommon issues:\n- `Connection refused on 127.0.0.1:9092` → Kafka not running\n- `Topic 'booking-updates' not found` → Topic needs to be created\n- `Serialization error` → Message format mismatch"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Flight Service Logs Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://example.com",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": ["example", "com"]
            },
            "description": "Check flight service logs for:\n\n1. **Kafka Connection**: \"Spring Kafka consumer configured\"\n2. **Message Consumption**: \"Received message from booking-updates topic\"\n3. **Seat Updates**: SQL update statements showing seat count changes\n4. **Errors**: Any JSON deserialization issues\n\nLook for patterns like:\n```\n[FlightService] Received booking event: flightId=1, passengerCount=2, isBusinessClass=false\n[FlightService] Updating flight 1 seats: economy -2\n```"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
